# ShotAnte env — see README "Deploy to Render" for the full runbook.
# Local dev needs NONE of these (in-memory, wagers off).

# ── game server (Render Web Service) ────────────────────────────────────────
# PORT is injected by Render automatically.
# NODE_VERSION=22

# Postgres audit log + player stats (Supabase pooler URL). Optional but
# required before real wagers — it's the dispute audit trail.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@host:5432/postgres

# Wagers: off (default) | mock (protocol tests, no chain) | chain (real)
# WAGER_MODE=off

# chain mode only — from `npm run deploy:escrow` output:
# CHAIN=baseSepolia                # baseSepolia | base | anvil (local rehearsal)
# ESCROW_ADDRESS=0x…
# SETTLEMENT_PRIVATE_KEY=0x…       # signs results ONLY; never holds funds.
#                                  # Secret store only — never commit, never reuse.
# RPC_URL=                         # recommended in production (public RPC rate-limits)
# (WAGER_TOKEN / WAGER_AMOUNT are gone — the stake is now a per-game fixed tier:
#  the host picks $0.10/$1/$5/$10 + USDC or Base ETH in the UI. USDC maps directly;
#  ETH is converted from USD at match start via CoinGecko, below.)

# CoinGecko price feed — USD->ETH conversion for the ETH wager tiers.
# Demo key (CG- prefix) uses the x-cg-demo-api-key header + api.coingecko.com.
# COINGECKO_API_KEY=CG-…

# Etherscan V2 API key (OPTIONAL) — only used at deploy time to verify the
# MatchEscrow source on Basescan (one key works across chains incl. Base). Not a
# runtime dependency; unset = skip verification.
# ETHERSCAN_API_KEY=…

# Auto-payout relayer (recommended): a gas-funded hot wallet that submits
# MatchEscrow.settle() when a wagered match ends, PUSHING the pot to the winner
# in that tx — no claim transaction and no gas on the winner's side. It only
# relays an already-signed result, so it can never move funds to itself
# (compromise = gas-griefing at worst). Keep it separate from the settlement
# signer, fund it with a little ETH for gas (your protocol fee covers this), and
# top it up as needed. Unset -> winners fall back to claiming the pot themselves.
# RELAYER_PRIVATE_KEY=0x…

# Protocol fee (basis points; 250 = 2.5%, on-chain cap 1000 = 10%).
# chain mode reads the LIVE value from the contract at boot — this env is the
# mock-mode display value and the deploy-time default for deploy-escrow.mjs.
# FEE_BPS=250
# FEE_RECIPIENT=0x…                # treasury that accrues fees (deploy + claim-fees.mjs)
# FEE_RECIPIENT_KEY=0x…            # ONLY for `npm run claim:fees` — withdraws accrued fees

# Gas sponsorship (OPTIONAL — only for the ANTE side): the relayer above already
# covers the claim side, and ETH antes need no help (the player has ETH). This
# only matters if you accept USDC antes from wallets with no ETH for gas. If you
# want it, PAYMASTER_RPC_URL is any ERC-7677 paymaster endpoint (carries a secret
# key, stays server-side); the browser only calls our /api/paymaster proxy, which
# relays pm_getPaymasterStubData / pm_getPaymasterData. Provider-agnostic — point
# it at whatever paymaster you run/rent. Unset = wallets pay their own ante gas.
# PAYMASTER_RPC_URL=https://<your-erc7677-paymaster-endpoint>

# Mainnet sequence: forge tests green -> `npm run rehearse:anvil` -> Base
# Sepolia dress rehearsal -> audit -> deploy with tiny caps -> Basescan verify
# -> smoke-test one paid duel. Full runbook: contracts/README.md.

# ── web client (Render Static Site, build-time) ─────────────────────────────
# VITE_SERVER_URL=wss://<your-game-server>.onrender.com
# Point the client at the server's paymaster proxy to turn on sponsored gas.
# Must match the host serving the game server (the /api/paymaster route above).
# VITE_PAYMASTER_URL=https://<your-game-server>.onrender.com/api/paymaster
